From: Metavert LLC <jon@metavert.io>
Subject: [PATCH] mcomp-vm: show its own name and version

The command name in usage lines and help is mcomp-vm, `--version` prints
the Lume version and the mcomp-vm revision (0.7.2-mcomp.2), and the help
banner says what it is, "mcomp-vm 0.7.2-mcomp.2: metacomputer's build of
Lume 0.7.2", without Lume's logo. The native VM window and its menu use
the same name.
Nothing users depend on changes: the ~/.lume storage, the settings file,
the LUME_* environment variables, the serve API, the binary's file name,
and Lume.Version.current, which the API, the update check and telemetry
report.
---
 libs/lume/src/MCompVM.swift                  | 18 ++++++++++
 libs/lume/src/Main.swift                     | 16 ++++-----
 libs/lume/src/VM/NativeApplicationLoop.swift |  2 +-
 libs/lume/src/VM/VMDisplayPresenter.swift    |  4 +--
 libs/lume/tests/MCompVMNameTests.swift       | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 62 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libs/lume/src/MCompVM.swift
 create mode 100644 libs/lume/tests/MCompVMNameTests.swift

diff --git a/libs/lume/src/MCompVM.swift b/libs/lume/src/MCompVM.swift
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..723a098
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libs/lume/src/MCompVM.swift
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+/// How this build introduces itself.
+///
+/// mcomp-vm is metacomputer's build of Lume, made by Metavert, not by Cua.
+/// Only the name and version people see change: the command name in usage
+/// lines, `--version`, the help banner and the VM window's title. Everything
+/// else stays Lume's: the `~/.lume` storage, the settings file, the `LUME_*`
+/// environment variables, the `serve` API, and `Lume.Version.current`, which
+/// the API, the update check and telemetry keep reporting.
+enum MCompVM {
+    /// The command name shown in usage lines, help and window titles.
+    static let name = "mcomp-vm"
+
+    /// This build's revision on top of the Lume release (MCOMP_REVISION in UPSTREAM).
+    static let revision = 2
+
+    /// What `--version` prints: the Lume version, then `-mcomp.<revision>`.
+    static var version: String { "\(Lume.Version.current)-mcomp.\(revision)" }
+}
